# The Beauty Edit

## Project Description

**The Beauty Edit** is a beauty discovery and wishlist application designed for beauty lovers who enjoy exploring makeup and skincare products.

Users can browse products from external APIs, search by product name or brand, and filter products by category. They can save their favourite products to a personal wishlist, track whether they have purchased them, and remove items they no longer want.

The application also allows users to create their own beauty products in a separate personal collection. These custom products can be added, edited, and deleted. Wishlist items and custom products are saved using the browser's `localStorage`, so user data remains available after refreshing the page.

The goal of The Beauty Edit is to provide a simple, responsive, and visually appealing space for discovering and organising beauty products.

## Technologies Used

- React
- JavaScript
- CSS
- HTML
- Browser `localStorage`
- External REST APIs

## APIs

The application fetches product information from two APIs:

1. **Makeup API:** [https://makeup-api.herokuapp.com/api/v1/products.json](https://makeup-api.herokuapp.com/api/v1/products.json)
2. **DummyJSON Skincare API:** [https://dummyjson.com/products/category/skin-care](https://dummyjson.com/products/category/skin-care)

The API data is combined and displayed in the product browsing section.

The application uses `fetch()` to retrieve the data and handles loading and error states while the products are being requested.

## Main Features

### Product Discovery
- Browse makeup and skincare products.
- Display products using reusable product cards.
- Search by product name or brand.
- Filter products by All, Makeup, or Skincare.
- Paginate product results.
- Handle unavailable product images with a fallback.

### Personal Wishlist
- Add products to a personal wishlist.
- Prevent duplicate products from being added.
- View saved product information.
- Track purchased and not-purchased items.
- Remove products from the wishlist.
- Save wishlist data using `localStorage`.

### My Beauty Collection
- Create custom beauty products.
- Add a product title, brand, category, and price.
- View user-created products separately from API products.
- Edit custom products.
- Delete custom products.
- Save custom products using `localStorage`.

## User Stories

**User Story 1 – Discover Products**

As a beauty shopper, I want to browse makeup and skincare products so that I can discover products I may want to purchase.

**User Story 2 – Search and Filter**

As a user, I want to search for products by name or brand and filter by category so that I can find products more easily.

**User Story 3 – Manage My Wishlist**

As a beauty enthusiast, I want to save products to my wishlist, track their purchase status, and remove products so that I can keep track of items I am interested in buying.

**User Story 4 – Manage Custom Products**

As a user, I want to create, edit, and delete my own beauty products so that I can maintain a personal beauty collection.

## Component Structure

The application is organised into reusable React components:

```text
THE BEAUTY EDIT
│
├── App.jsx
│   │
│   ├── Header
│   ├── HeroSection
│   │
│   ├── BrowserSection
│   │   ├── SearchBar
│   │   ├── CategoryFilter
│   │   └── ProductList
│   │       └── ProductCard
│   │
│   ├── WishlistSection
│   │   └── WishlistCard
│   │
│   ├── AddProductForm
│   ├── CustomProductList
│   ├── EditProductForm
│   │
│   └── Footer
│
└── main.jsx
```

## State Management

The application uses React's `useState` and `useEffect` hooks to manage product data, user interactions, API requests, and data persistence.

